    The preferred universal location, promised permanent. "This will keep resolving." A standing commitment by the naming authority — breaking it is a breach, not an event.
  ; Suspended, not deleted: under D11 the parent concept re-carved as
  ; universal-path; whether the promise classes are now PATH-promises is
  ; the expressly un-adjudicated knock-on (def-entities-values-promises WN).
  |set-rel :kind subset-of :to @universal-path :status pending-adjudication :cite D11
  |set-rel :kind disjoint-from :to @preferred-location
  |confused
    :with @preferred-location
    Canonical carries a permanence promise; preferred may be superseded without breach. The difference is the promise, not the string.
